<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Fangtou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">369</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Fangtou was fought in 369 in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/former-yan">Former Yan</a> general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-chui">Murong Chui</a> defeated the northern expedition of the Eastern Jin commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huan-wen">Huan Wen</a> near Fangtou, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>. Huan Wen's army, short of supplies, retreated and lost many thousands of men. The victory saved Former Yan for the moment, but court jealousy then drove <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-xianbei">Murong</a> Chui to flee to the Former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a>.</p></div>
